# Combinator and string method status ({{pin.version}})

Story 131.2; re-measured in full for story 136.53; generated since 136.58.

**This document is rendered from a measurement, not written by hand.** Every
verdict cell — `--check`, `build`, `runs`, `correct` — and the pin below are
rendered by `scripts/render_combinator_status.py` from
`patterns/probe/probe_results.json`, which `patterns/probe/run_probes.sh`
produces by compiling and running one complete program per probe. The notes
column and the prose are hand-written, in the template
`patterns/probe/combinator-status.md.tmpl`. Every probe appears in some row,
and every row names the probes behind it; a row whose probes disagree does not
render.

Until 136.58 every row was transcribed from the JSON by hand, and on
2026-09-22 roughly twenty of them described a compiler from before
127.4/127.6/127.7/127.10 and 137.12 landed, **every one claiming breakage that
no longer existed**, while the JSON beside them was correct. `make ci` now
fails when this file differs from its rendering (`check-combinator-status`)
and when a fresh probe run disagrees with the committed JSON
(`check-probes`). To change a verdict, change the compiler and re-run
`make render-combinator-status PROBES=1`; to change a note, edit the template.

## Measurement pin

